  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_096",
  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/leichhardt/Leichhardt DCP 2013 - 11 - Part F Food - with IWLEP 2022 amendments.pdf\n\nClause Section 1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): appropriate composting and waste management (see Council’s website for information on minimising waste and composting guidelines); and\n\nClause Section 1 - other (environmental_protection): the need to consider the quality of soil in relation to potential contamination.\n\nClause F1.1 FOOD PRODUCTION - other (environmental_protection): Council’s approach and responsibilities for contaminated land management are outlined within Part C1.8 Contamination of this Development Control Plan.\n\nClause F1.1 FOOD PRODUCTION - other (environmental_protection): The Development Control Plan creates the framework to ensure that while carrying out its planning functions, Council considers the possibility that a previous land use or environmental factors surrounding a specific site have caused contamination at the site.\n\nClause F1.1 FOOD PRODUCTION - other (environmental_protection): healthy soil is to be maintained through the incorporation of compost and well-rotted manure without excess nitrogen\n\nClause F1.1 FOOD PRODUCTION - other (environmental_protection): plant diversity should be maintained through the planting of both native and exotic species that are not weed species, and are not an exempt species as listed in Part C1.14 – Tree Management within this Development Control Plan\n\nClause F1.1 FOOD PRODUCTION - other (environmental_protection): Council supports the use of organic and chemical free agricultural practice in pest management and plant maintenance.\n\nClause F1.1.3 Community gardens - development_application (development_control): Applicants are to submit a development application to Council for development of a Community Garden on private land or land owned by or control vested in Council.\n\n",
